        <td class="NewsText" style="font-size: 15px">The <a href="mx">MX Linux</a> project has published a new update to the 25.x series. Along with importing new security fixes and firmware from its Debian parent, the MX Linux project includes a number of new changes: "<span class="Quote">On the MX side, we have pushed most of our updates as we’ve gone along, but there are some specific updates of note this time around. MX-Welcome, MX-Tools and custom-toolbox (used by Fluxbox) received user interface facelifts. Verify-iso-sig, a new tool for verifying digital signatures for not only MX ISOs, but also isos from many popular distribution families. MX-Theme-Colors, a fun tool for creating custom-highlight themes from existing MX themes (GTK). Introduction of siduction 7.X kernels in mx-packageinstaller-&gt;popular apps-&gt;kernels Many updates to the third-party vpn installers in mx-packageinstaller-&gt;popular apps mx/gazelle-installer will set up lazytime in fstab by default (new installations). Updated manual and FAQ entries
